IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- National Rental Affordability Scheme Act 2008 (Cth) — THE NOUNS, THE RULES
-- AND THE TOP-LEVEL GOAL. Source: ../registers/source-bundle/C2008A00121.txt
-- (compilation No. 4, 5 December 2025). The investor who owns an NRAS
-- dwelling asks: "Is it a rental dwelling; does it meet the Act's conditions
-- of an allocation this year; when does the incentive period end, and which
-- NRAS year am I in?"

§ `Nouns`

-- s 4 rental dwelling.
DECLARE `Kind of dwelling` IS ONE OF
    `a dwelling, or a part capable of being lived in as a separate residence`
    `a strata unit`
    `a caravan, houseboat or other mobile dwelling`
    `a dwelling the regulations exclude`

DECLARE `Dwelling case` HAS
    `the kind of dwelling`                                  IS A `Kind of dwelling`
    `rent is payable for it`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 4 incentive period: 10 years starting on or after 1 July 2008
    `the incentive period starts on`                        IS A DATE
    -- s 7(2)(a)
    `it was lived in as a residence before the period began` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was unfit, and not lived in from being made fit to the period's start` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 7(2)(b)
    `it was rented in the year`                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `the tenants are of the prescribed kind`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the rent charges in the year`                          IS A LIST OF NUMBER
    `the market value rent for the same period`             IS A NUMBER
    -- s 7(5)
    `the Secretary disapplied the rent condition`           IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 7(2)(c)
    `the longest vacancy in the year, in days`              IS A NUMBER
    `the longest vacancy the regulations allow, in days`    IS A NUMBER
    -- s 4 NRAS year
    `the day asked about`                                   IS A DATE

DECLARE `Dwelling position` HAS
    `it is a rental dwelling under s 4`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the incentive period ends on`                          IS A DATE
    `the newness condition of s 7(2)(a) is met`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `the rent condition is met this year`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the tenant or vacancy condition is met this year`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the NRAS year starts on`                               IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the NRAS year ends on`                                 IS A MAYBE DATE

§ `Rules`

@ref s 4 rental dwelling
GIVEN c IS A `Dwelling case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a rental dwelling` c IF
        c's `rent is payable for it`
    AND (   c's `the kind of dwelling` EQUALS `a dwelling, or a part capable of being lived in as a separate residence`
         OR c's `the kind of dwelling` EQUALS `a strata unit`)

-- s 4 incentive period: "a 10 year period": it ends on the day before the
-- tenth anniversary of its first day, or at the month's end where there is
-- none (changed after the independent pass).
@ref s 4 incentive period
GIVEN c IS A `Dwelling case`
GIVETH A DATE
`the end of the incentive period for` c MEANS
    IF DATE_DAY (`add months` start 120) LESS THAN DATE_DAY start
    THEN `add months` start 120
    ELSE `the day before` (`add months` start 120)
    WHERE
        start MEANS c's `the incentive period starts on`

-- s 7(2)(a): not lived in as a residence before the incentive period, or, if
-- unfit, not lived in between being made fit and the period's first day.
@ref s 7(2)(a), (3)
GIVEN c IS A `Dwelling case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the newness condition is met` c IF
        NOT (c's `it was lived in as a residence before the period began`)
    OR  c's `it was unfit, and not lived in from being made fit to the period's start`

-- s 7(2)(b)(ii): each charge at least 20% less than the market value rent;
-- s 7(5): unless the Secretary disapplies it.
@ref s 7(2)(b)(ii), (5)
GIVEN c IS A `Dwelling case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the rent condition is met` c IF
        NOT (c's `it was rented in the year`)
    OR  c's `the Secretary disapplied the rent condition`
    OR  all (GIVEN r YIELD r AT MOST 8/10 TIMES c's `the market value rent for the same period`) (c's `the rent charges in the year`)

-- s 7(2)(b)(i): rented to prescribed tenants; s 7(2)(c): when not rented, not
-- vacant longer than the regulations allow.
@ref s 7(2)(b)(i), (c)
GIVEN c IS A `Dwelling case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the tenant or vacancy condition is met` c IF
    IF c's `it was rented in the year`
    THEN     c's `the tenants are of the prescribed kind`
         AND c's `the longest vacancy in the year, in days` AT MOST c's `the longest vacancy the regulations allow, in days`
    ELSE c's `the longest vacancy in the year, in days` AT MOST c's `the longest vacancy the regulations allow, in days`

-- s 4 NRAS year: 1 July 2008 to 30 April 2009, then years from 1 May.
@ref s 4 NRAS year
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the NRAS year start for` d MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF d LESS THAN Date 1 7 2008 THEN NOTHING
        IF d AT MOST Date 30 4 2009 THEN JUST (Date 1 7 2008)
        IF DATE_MONTH d AT LEAST 5 THEN JUST (Date 1 5 (DATE_YEAR d))
        OTHERWISE JUST (Date 1 5 (DATE_YEAR d MINUS 1))

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the NRAS year end for` d MEANS
    CONSIDER `the NRAS year start for` d
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST s THEN
        IF s EQUALS Date 1 7 2008 THEN JUST (Date 30 4 2009)
        ELSE JUST (Date 30 4 (DATE_YEAR s PLUS 1))

@ref ss 4, 7
@export default The position of the investor who owns a dwelling under the National Rental Affordability Scheme Act 2008 (Cth): whether it is a rental dwelling (not a caravan, houseboat or other mobile dwelling: s 4); when the 10-year incentive period ends; and whether the Act's own conditions of an allocation are met (s 7(2)): the dwelling was new, or not lived in since being made fit, at the start of the period; in a year it is rented, the tenants are of the prescribed kind and every rent charge is at least 20% below market value rent (unless the Secretary has disapplied that); and it was not vacant longer than the regulations allow; with the NRAS year (from 1 May, the first ran 1 July 2008 to 30 April 2009). DRAFT, not reviewed by an Australian lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Dwelling case`  @desc The dwelling, the incentive period's start, when it was first lived in or made fit, this year's tenants, rents, market rent and vacancy, and the day asked about
GIVETH A `Dwelling position`
`the dwelling position for` c MEANS
    `Dwelling position` OF `it is a rental dwelling` c, `the end of the incentive period for` c, `the newness condition is met` c,
                           `the rent condition is met` c, `the tenant or vacancy condition is met` c,
                           `the NRAS year start for` (c's `the day asked about`), `the NRAS year end for` (c's `the day asked about`)
